  7 | run: fn() { _: fmt.ordinal(3) }
    |                    ^^^^^^^
 Why: `core.text.fmt.ordinal` allocates at Fmt.jet:32: string interpolation allocates a new `String`; on a machine with no heap, nothing the program reaches may allocate, in Core and packages as in its own code
 Fix: Select a target machine with an allocator, or call a heap-free operation instead.
 Denial: invocation
 Call chain: run → ordinal
